::: {.cell-output-display}
![Changes (days/year) in predicted dates of first adult emergence for PTLM across the CONUS over the entire 44-year period (1981–2025). Maps show (A) all changes and (B) statistically significant changes (P < 0.1); areas shown in gray are not statistically significant.](figure1.png){#fig-ptlm-emergence fig-align='center' width=70%}
:::
:::



::: {.cell layout-align="center"}
::: {.cell-output-display}
![Changes (days/year) in predicted dates of first egg hatch for PTLM across the CONUS over the entire 44-year period (1981–2025). Maps show (A) all changes and (B) statistically significant changes (P < 0.1); areas shown in gray are not statistically significant.](figure2.png){#fig-ptlm-egg-hatch fig-align='center' width=70%}
:::
:::


#### **Recent period: 2001--2025**

During 2001–2025, predicted egg hatch generally shifted earlier across much of the western and central United States, whereas adult emergence showed a more mixed pattern, including later events across portions of the northern and central interior (@fig-ptlm-emergence-recent, @fig-ptlm-egg-hatch-recent). Significant changes were spatially limited.


