![Changes (days/year) in predicted dates of first egg hatch for PTLM across the CONUS over the recent 24-year period (2001–2025). Maps show (A) all changes and (B) statistically significant changes (P < 0.1); areas shown in gray are not statistically significant.](figure4.png){#fig-ptlm-egg-hatch-recent fig-align='center' width=70%}
:::
:::


### **ii. Climatic suitability**

#### **Entire period: 1981--2025**

Predicted cold stress decreased across much of the northern United States over 1981–2025, while heat stress increased broadly across the western and southern United States (@fig-ptlm-cold-stress, @fig-ptlm-heat-stress). Significant increases in climatic suitability occurred across portions of the central and eastern United States, with additional localized areas in the West (@fig-ptlm-suitability).


::: {.cell layout-align="center"}
::: {.cell-output-display}
![Changes (units/year) in predicted cold stress for PTLM across the CONUS over the entire 44-year period (1981–2025). Maps show (A) all changes and (B) statistically significant changes (P < 0.1); areas shown in gray are not statistically significant. Areas shown as 0 in (B) had significant trends but very small changes.](figure5.png){#fig-ptlm-cold-stress fig-align='center' width=70%}
:::
:::



::: {.cell layout-align="center"}
::: {.cell-output-display}
![Changes (units/year) in predicted heat stress for PTLM across the CONUS over the entire 44-year period (1981–2025). Maps show (A) all changes and (B) statistically significant changes (P < 0.1); areas shown in gray are not statistically significant. Areas shown as 0 in (B) had significant trends but very small changes.](figure6.png){#fig-ptlm-heat-stress fig-align='center' width=70%}
:::
:::



